      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your review. According to your reply, fuse_handle_backing receives fi-\u003ebacking_inode as an input param and replaces it with backing_file-\u003ef_inode. \nHowever, when new_backing_inode \u003d NULL, the origin codes listed below lead to panic in function ihold.\n\nnew_backing_inode \u003d fi-\u003ebacking_inode;\nihold(new_backing_inode);  // Actually ihold(NULL)\n\nvoid ihold(struct inode *inode)\n{\n     WARN_ON(atomic_inc_return(\u0026inode-\u003ei_count) \u003c 2); // NULL pointer dereference occurs when inode is NULL\n}\n\nTo avoid the panic, is it a good idea to check whether new_backing_inode is NULL or not before ihold(new_backing_inode);",
